# Prop Ordering

For React components, keep props sorted alphabetically to reduce diff noise and
make scanning easier.

- Sort prop keys alphabetically in prop types/interfaces.
- Sort destructured function props alphabetically in component signatures.
- Keep the same alphabetical order when forwarding many props.
- If a grouping is required for readability, add a short comment explaining why.

Example:

```tsx
type ExampleProps = {
  addressSearch: string;
  dialogOpen: boolean;
  fields: AddressFields;
  manualMode: boolean;
}

function Example({
  addressSearch,
  dialogOpen,
  fields,
  manualMode,
}: ExampleProps) {}
```
